# Inventory module

**Read the full memory model first:** [`.cursor/rules/docs/inventory-module.md`](docs/inventory-module.md)

Match the party module CRUD template ([`backend/src/party/`](../backend/src/party/)): thin controllers, `prisma.client` for reads, `unitOfWork.run` for writes, audit + outbox in the same transaction.

## Golden rules

1. **Never** mutate `Stock.availableQuantity` directly — use `InventoryLedgerService.applyMovement` only.
2. **`StockMovement` is immutable** — read-only API; ledger creates movements.
3. **`Batch` is org-global**; `Stock`, adjustments, stock-takes are **branch-scoped** via `RequestContext`.
4. Document numbers from `SequenceGeneratorService` inside `unitOfWork.run`.
5. Nested items: parent FK from **route param**, not create body (no `items[]` on header create).

## Status machines

| Document | Flow | Workflow routes |
|----------|------|-----------------|
| StockAdjustment | DRAFT → APPROVED | `POST :id/approve` |
| StockTransfer | DRAFT → DISPATCHED → COMPLETED / PARTIALLY_RECEIVED | `POST :id/dispatch`, `POST :id/receive` |
| StockTake | DRAFT → IN_PROGRESS → COUNTED → RECONCILED | `POST :id/start`, `POST :id/complete`, `POST :id/reconcile` |

Header/item edits and deletes only in **DRAFT** (`assertDraftStatus`). Stock-take items also allow CRUD when parent is `IN_PROGRESS`.

## Layer checklist

- **DTOs:** update requires `version`; no server-managed fields on create; signed qty only on adjustment items.
- **Mappers:** one-way `to{Entity}Response()`; IDs as strings; `serializeDecimal` for decimals.
- **Services:** optimistic lock via `updateMany` + `optimisticUpdate()`; workflow guards before ledger calls.
- **Permissions:** `INVENTORY:RESOURCE:ACTION` on every endpoint (`@RequirePermissions`).
- **Constants/enums:** [`inventory.constants.ts`](../backend/src/inventory/constants/inventory.constants.ts).
- **Utils:** [`inventory.util.ts`](../backend/src/inventory/utils/inventory.util.ts) — asserts, serializers.

## Workflow ledger (summary)

- Approve adjustment → `ADJUSTMENT_GAIN` / `ADJUSTMENT_LOSS` per item
- Dispatch transfer → `TRANSFER_OUT` at source branch
- Receive transfer → `TRANSFER_IN` at destination (`receivedQuantity ?? sentQuantity`)
- Reconcile stock-take → auto-approved adjustment + ledger for non-zero variances

## Not implemented

